    Quote: However, the company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. Designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, Kyber is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system and a key component of Nvidia's long-term AI infrastructure strategy.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e256 (); both are in force: Research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks; the item says this could push NVIDIA to lean further on its new credit and revenue-sharing model to sustain demand.\",\n   \"- e316 [party_statement; IEEE Spectrum; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a4eb2bdfabca94f5887881c6 2026-07-09] NVIDIA is planning to add more processors to its single interconnected systems, scaling from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 GPUs by 2027, according to IEEE Spectrum.\\n    Quote: At the same time, Nvidia is planning to add even more processors to single interconnected systems, going from 72 GPUs today to as many as 576 by 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e257; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e334 [party_statement; moomoo; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] NVIDIA issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay and confirming that its product roadmap remains intact.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA recently issued a statement to Bloomberg denying claims of a technical delay, confirming that its product roadmap remains intact. This clarification serves as a counterweight to concerns that infrastructure bottlenecks could disrupt the company’s competitive lead in the artificial intelligence sector.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber rack system is delayed, stating that 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109, e129, e173, e189, e204, e220, e302, e334, e385; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e256 [third_party_view; futuriom.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks; the item says this could push NVIDIA to lean further on its new credit and revenue-sharing model to sustain demand.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s stock also suffered this week because research firm SemiAnalysis stated in an X post that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has hit manufacturing setbacks—a situation that could be further impetus for NVIDIA to deploy its new credit and revenue-sharing model, creating a continuing flow of demand for its products.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e384 [rumour; Jim Cramer (via finance.yahoo.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] Reports circulated that NVIDIA's next-generation AI chips face delays; per Jim Cramer, SemiAnalysis reported that \\\"everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late,\\\" in the context of what the article calls the Kyber delay. The reports are contested (see NVIDIA's denial in a separate item).\\n    Quote: AI giant NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) is currently in the news these days due to reports of a delay to its next generation AI chips. … You know Semi Analysis does pretty good work, saying that everything could be late for NVIDIA because one particular part of their business is late.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e256; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e385 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corp. ; from gnews:1c3c0c58ed5ec3da43292f9b 2026-07-11] NVIDIA Corp. denied reports that its Kyber platform is being delayed, asserting that its product plan/schedule stands.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has denied reports that the Kyber platform is being delayed.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported in a post published Monday that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, which is designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028 because the specialized multi-layer PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture; the larger NVL576 system linking eight racks via optical connections is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e107, e125, e126, e167, e172, e176, e182, e184, e203, e219, e301, e419; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber rack system is delayed, stating that 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109, e129, e173, e189, e204, e220, e302, e334, e385, e420; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e419 [third_party_view; Geoffrey Seiler (fool.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] Technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 next-generation AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of difficulties in manufacturing a crucial circuit board, as recounted by fool.com's Geoffrey Seiler, who notes NVIDIA's rack-scale strategy is central to CEO Jensen Huang's plan.\\n    Quote: This has been a key part of CEO Jensen Huang's strategy; however, it could have hit a snag when technology research outfit SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e420 [party_statement; Geoffrey Seiler (fool.com); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] NVIDIA responded to SemiAnalysis's report that its Kyber NVL144 rack could slip to 2028 by saying its roadmap remains intact, though the article says questions linger; no schedule or shipment date was given.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact, although questions linger.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e430 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said, in investor-relations discussions reported by gurufocus.com on 2026-07-13, that development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule and confirmed there have been no changes to its NVLink architecture.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e128 (); both are in force: A week before the Kyber report, SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design, also due to 'manufacturing execution concerns.' The two-die offering will deliver around half the performance of the four-die Rubin Ultra.\",\n   \"- e91 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] Research firm SemiAnalysis reported in a post published Monday that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack-scale architecture, which is designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028 because the specialized multi-layer PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture; the larger NVL576 system linking eight racks via optical connections is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis, the latest in a string of reported setbacks raising questions about the AI giant's product roadmap. … The setback stems from difficulties manufacturing a key circuit board at the heart of the syst\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e107, e125, e126, e167, e172, e176, e182, e184, e203, e219, e301, e419, e540; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis's report that its next-generation Kyber rack system is delayed, stating that 'Our roadmap is intact.'\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e109, e129, e173, e189, e204, e220, e302, e334, e385, e420, e541; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e540 [third_party_view; EBC (ebc.com); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Industry research firm SemiAnalysis reported over the weekend that Nvidia's upcoming Kyber NVL144 rack architecture could face delays extending into 2028, according to reports the article describes as unverified rumors.\\n    Quote: Over the weekend, reports circulated from industry research firm SemiAnalysis suggesting that Nvidia’s upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e541 [party_statement; Nvidia spokesperson, reported by EBC (ebc.com); original source NVIDIA Corp. ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An Nvidia spokesperson countered the SemiAnalysis delay report, telling reporters that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact\\\".\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" the seeds of doubt were already sown.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e393 (); both are in force: Multiple reports, led by The Information and corroborated through September 2026, say NVIDIA has shipped no new gaming GPU architecture in calendar 2026 — the first blank year since the GeForce 256 debut in October 1999. NVIDIA reportedly shelved its entire planned RTX 50 'Super' refresh in December 2025, including a 24GB RTX 5080 Super that had reached completed-design stage, and its next-generation RTX 60-series (Rubin-based) has slipped from a rumored late-2027 launch to 2028. NVIDIA has not confirmed the skip on the record, only acknowledging memory supply constraints in a statement to Tom's Hardware.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
